<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shimashki dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shimashki</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shimashki dynasty was a line of rulers from the Iranian highlands who dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> around the end of the third millennium BCE. Its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kindattu">Kindattu</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a> around 2004 BCE and took the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a> captive. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> treat this as ending Mesopotamian hegemony over Elam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shimashki-dynasty.jpg" alt="Shimashki dynasty" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Enyavar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Near_East_2000BC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
